<div class="help-article">
    <p class="help-lead">
        Help is in two places: this page, which holds every article and searches them, and the
        <span class="help-icon help-icon-help help-icon-inline" aria-hidden="true"></span> button at the top of every page,
        which opens the article about the page you're on.
    </p>
    <HelpClip Name="help-using" Caption="Opening the Import page's help, then searching every article." />

    <h3>The help button</h3>
    <p>
        The <span class="help-icon help-icon-help help-icon-inline" aria-hidden="true"></span> button sits in the blue bar at the
        top right. It opens the article for the current page in a window over it, so you keep your place. Press
        <kbd>Esc</kbd>, click outside it or choose <span class="help-ui">Close</span> to get back. <span class="help-ui">All help topics</span>
        at its foot brings you here.
    </p>

    <h3>Searching</h3>
    <p>
        Type in the search box at the top of this page. It looks at the titles, the one-line summaries and a list of words
        behind each article, and narrows the list as you type. Each extra word narrows it further. Press <kbd>Esc</kbd> to
        clear it. Short words work best: <em>pdf</em>, <em>receipt</em>, <em>rrsp</em>, <em>backup</em>, <em>duplicate</em>.
    </p>

    <h3>Browsing</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>The chips under the search box show one section at a time; <span class="help-ui">All</span> shows everything.</li>
        <li>Click an article's title to open it, and again to close it. Several can be open at once.</li>
        <li><span class="help-ui">Expand all</span> opens every article listed, handy for reading or printing the lot.</li>
        <li>Each article ends with a link to the page it describes.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
